Sony calibration data
---------------------

LLR reproduces the rendering of Sony's RAW converter. To do so it ships tables
that were read out of Sony's Imaging Edge Desktop ("Edit") or out of RAW files
written by Sony cameras, rather than authored here:

  apps/worker/src/llr_worker/sony/data/   (tone, luma, 3-D LUT, hue and look tables)
  apps/web/public/sony-lut3d.bin
  apps/web/public/sony-tone-family.bin

The test fixtures under apps/worker/tests/fixtures/, apps/web/scripts/ and
apps/web/src/rendering/__tests__/, and the measurement data under sony_repro/,
were likewise captured from that software's input and output, to check this
project's implementation against it.

These files remain the property of their owner. They are included for
interoperability with files produced by Sony cameras. apps/worker/src/
llr_worker/sony/data/camera_match.json is the exception: it is a correction
fitted by this project against camera JPEGs, and is covered by the MIT License.

Not included
------------

Adobe DNG camera profiles (used for non-Sony RAWs) are not distributed; the
README says how to supply your own copy. The models LLR can download at run
time (generative erase, relight geometry, AI masks) are fetched from their
publishers and are subject to their own licenses.

